This directory vendors a minimal subset of BasicSR — only what
RestoreFormer++ (core/face_restorer.py) and NAFNet (core/deblur.py) actually
need at inference time, not the training framework, dataset registry, or
CUDA ops.

basicsr/utils/{img_util,logger,dist_util}.py, basicsr/__init__.py:
  Source: https://github.com/XPixelGroup/BasicSR (v1.4.2)
  License: Apache License 2.0 (see UPSTREAM_LICENSE)

basicsr/models/archs/{NAFNet_arch,arch_util}.py:
  These two files are NOT from XPixelGroup/BasicSR upstream — they're from
  megvii-research/NAFNet, which forked BasicSR and added them under this
  same basicsr.models.archs namespace. Vendored as-is (NAFNet_arch.py trimmed
  — see its own header comment).
  Source: https://github.com/megvii-research/NAFNet
  License: MIT License (see UPSTREAM_LICENSE_NAFNET)

Vendored instead of pip-installed because the upstream basicsr PyPI sdist's
setup.py fails on modern setuptools (KeyError: '__version__', an unfixed
upstream packaging bug unrelated to this project) — this affects both the
XPixelGroup and megvii-research forks identically, since they share the
same broken setup.py.
